course: dictionary
lesson: 3128
title: Elegant: graceful, stylish and clever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Elegant describes something that moves or looks graceful, stylish and beautiful. Look at the words around it for clues: «The swan glided across the lake, elegant and calm.» Graceful and calm tell you that elegant means smooth and lovely to watch.
explain: Elegant can also describe things that are fine and tasteful, such as clothes, buildings and handwriting. «The Dodo gave a gift, with an elegant thimble.» Here the word shows that the thimble is a fine, pretty and carefully chosen gift.
explain: In maths or science, elegant means simple, clever and neat. «An elegant solution» solves a problem in a short, smart way. To check your meaning, swap in a word such as «smart and simple» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Elegant is an adjective. Its forms are more elegant and most elegant.
fact: «Elegant» means graceful and stylish, or fine and tasteful.
fact: In maths and science, «elegant» means simple, clever and neat.
fact: «Elegantly simple» means something is both easy to understand and beautifully clever.
fact: You can check an unknown word by swapping in your meaning and reading the sentence again.
exercise: «The swan glided across the lake, elegant and calm.» What does elegant mean here? | Loud and noisy | Tired from swimming | Dirty and wet | *Graceful and stylish
exercise: A maths teacher says, «That is an elegant solution.» What does elegant mean? | Written in pencil | Wrong but quick | Long and messy | *Simple, clever and neat
exercise: Which word could replace elegant in «She wore an elegant dress to the party»? | Muddy | Noisy | Torn | *Stylish and tasteful
test: What is the best meaning of elegant in «an elegant solution»? | Loud | Long and boring | Hidden | *Simple, clever and neat
test: What is the opposite of elegant, meaning graceful? | Fine | Stylish | *Clumsy | Graceful
exam: Which sentence uses elegant to mean graceful? | «Tom ate a cold sandwich.» | «The elephant stomped through the mud.» | «The bell rang at noon.» | *«The dancer moved with elegant steps across the stage.»
